+The clinic publishes the veterinarians it employs with the specialties each holds, listed a page at a time. A veterinarian holding no specialty is shown as having none rather than left blank `[REQ-VET-001]`. The same directory is also published in a machine-readable form at a second address; that machine-readable surface is a supported capability, and filtering by specialty is its first requested one `[REQ-VET-003]`.
+
+Either surface accepts an optional specialty filter. When a specialty is named, the directory presents only the veterinarians holding that specialty, matched against the whole specialty name and disregarding letter case rather than matching a prefix. On the page-at-a-time surface the paging applies to the filtered set. A specialty that no veterinarian holds yields the ordinary directory with an empty list rather than an error. A filter that is blank or only spaces is treated as no filter at all, exactly as an empty owner search is. Without a filter, each surface presents the whole directory `[REQ-VET-003]`.
 
 **Done when:**
 - `[REQ-VET-001]` given the clinic's veterinarians, when the directory is opened, then each name and its specialties are listed a page at a time.
 - `[REQ-VET-001]` given a veterinarian holding no specialty, when the directory is opened, then that veterinarian is shown as having none.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a specialty that some veterinarians hold, when either surface is filtered by that specialty, then only those veterinarians are presented, and the machine-readable surface returns them with a success response.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a specialty name differing from a stored one only by letter case, when either surface is filtered by it, then it matches; given only the start of a stored specialty name, when either surface is filtered by it, then it does not match.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a specialty that no veterinarian holds, when either surface is filtered by it, then the ordinary directory is returned with an empty veterinarian list and a success response.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a blank or whitespace-only filter, when either surface receives it, then the whole directory is presented as though no filter were given.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given no filter, when either surface is opened, then it presents the whole directory as before.
 
 **Edge cases:**
 1. A veterinarian's specialties are presented in a stable order rather than an arbitrary one.
-2. **Known defect.** A second route returns the same list in a machine-readable form. Nothing consumes it, and it carries no requirement — see the Superseded list.
+2. On the page-at-a-time surface, paging counts only the veterinarians the filter matches, not the whole directory.
+3. A blank or whitespace-only filter returns the whole directory, distinct from a named specialty that matches nobody, which returns an empty list.
 
 **Design:** [system-design.md#contracts](system-design.md#contracts)
 
